      "id": 1,
      "text": "The Hudson River Railroad Company laid track along the east shore of the Hudson in 1850, forever changing access to the waterway.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://historian.columbiacountyny.com/municipal-historians/town-of-stuyvesant"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "By the turn of the century the steam-powered line was electrified and extended to Albany.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://historian.columbiacountyny.com/municipal-historians/town-of-stuyvesant"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In March 2026 Stuyvesant launched its Natural and Cultural Resources Inventory to map the town’s most significant natural, historic, scenic, and recreational resources.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://stuyvesantny.gov/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Spectacular views of the upper and lower falls are visible from the historic iron truss bridge that spans the creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
